localRing -- Constructor for local rings
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        R_P
        R_f
        localRing(R, P)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note polynomial ring: (Macaulay2Doc)PolynomialRing,, the base
        ring for the localization
      * P, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a prime ideal for the
        localization
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, a ring element to
        localize (not yet implemented)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note local ring: LocalRing,, the local ring $R_{\mathfrac p}$

Description
===========

This is the constructor for the type *note LocalRing: LocalRing,.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,w];                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = ideal"xz-y2,yw-z2,xw-yz"; -- The twisted cubic curve      |
|                                                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal"xz-y2,z(yw-z2)-w(xw-yz)";                           |
|                                                                   |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : RP = R_P                                                      |
|                                                                   |
|o4 = RP                                                            |
|                                                                   |
|                                  2           2                    |
|o4 : LocalRing, maximal ideal (- y  + x*z, - z  + y*w, - y*z + x*w)|
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = RP^1/promote(I, RP)                                       |
|                                                                   |
|o5 = cokernel | -y2+xz -z3+2yzw-xw2 |                              |
|                                                                   |
|                              1                                    |
|o5 : RP-module, quotient of RP                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : length M                                                      |
|                                                                   |
|o6 = 2                                                             |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+

Note that the ideal $P$ is assumed to be prime. Use *note
isWellDefined(LocalRing): isWellDefined_lpLocalRing_rp, to confirm that a local
ring is well defined.



