isWellDefined(LocalRing) -- whether a local ring is well defined
****************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,

Description
===========

This method checks whether the local ring was produced by localization at a
prime ideal.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z,w]                                         |
|                                                             |
|o1 = R                                                       |
|                                                             |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : P = ideal"xz-y2,yw-z2,xw-yz"; -- The twisted cubic curve|
|                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isWellDefined R_P                                       |
|                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : Q = ideal"xz-y2,z(yw-z2)-w(xw-yz)";                     |
|                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : isWellDefined R_Q                                       |
|                                                             |
|o5 = false                                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
