hilbertSamuelFunction -- Computes the Hilbert-Samuel Function of Modules over Local Rings
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        h = hilbertSamuelFunction(M, n)
        L = hilbertSamuelFunction(M, n0, n1)
        h = hilbertSamuelFunction(q, M, n)
        L = hilbertSamuelFunction(q, M, n0, n1)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, a module over a local ring
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, single input to the function
      * n0, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, first input to the function
      * n1, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, last input to the function
      * q, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a parameter ideal
  * Outputs:
      * h, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the integer output of the
        Hilbert-Samuel function
      * L, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, an sequence of integer
        outputs of the Hilbert-Samuel function

Description
===========

Given a module over a local ring, a parameter ideal, and an integer, this
method computes the Hilbert-Samuel function for the module. If parameter ideal
is not given, the maximal ideal is assumed.

Note: If computing at index n is fast but slows down at n+1, try computing at
range (n, n+1). On the other hand, if computing at range (n, n+m) is slow, try
breaking up the range.

To learn more read Eisenbud, Commutative Algebra, Chapter 12.

Here is an example from Computations in Algebraic Geometry with Macaulay2, pp.
61:

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : RP = localRing(R, ideal gens R);                |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal"x5+y3+z3,x3+y5+z3,x3+y3+z5"           |
|                                                     |
|             5    3    3   5    3    3   5    3    3 |
|o3 = ideal (x  + y  + z , y  + x  + z , z  + x  + y )|
|                                                     |
|o3 : Ideal of RP                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = RP^1/I                                      |
|                                                     |
|o4 = cokernel | x5+y3+z3 y5+x3+z3 z5+x3+y3 |         |
|                                                     |
|                              1                      |
|o4 : RP-module, quotient of RP                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : elapsedTime hilbertSamuelFunction(M, 0, 6)      |
| -- .28363s elapsed                                  |
|                                                     |
|o5 = {1, 3, 6, 7, 6, 3, 1}                           |
|                                                     |
|o5 : List                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : oo//sum                                         |
|                                                     |
|o6 = 27                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

An example of using a parameter ideal:

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : R = ZZ/32003[x,y];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : RP = localRing(R, ideal gens R);                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : N = RP^1                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|       1                                                                     |
|o9 = RP                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : RP-module, free                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : q = ideal"x2,y3"                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|              2   3                                                          |
|o10 = ideal (x , y )                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o10 : Ideal of RP                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : elapsedTime hilbertSamuelFunction(N, 0, 5) -- n+1 -- 0.02 seconds      |
| -- .0165078s elapsed                                                        |
|                                                                             |
|o11 = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o11 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : elapsedTime hilbertSamuelFunction(q, N, 0, 5) -- 6(n+1) -- 0.32 seconds|
| -- .257452s elapsed                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o12 = {6, 12, 18, 24, 30, 36}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o12 : List                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Hilbert-Samuel function with respect to a parameter ideal other than the
maximal ideal can be slower.

See also
========

  * *note length(Module): (Macaulay2Doc)length_lpModule_rp, -- compute the
    length of a module

Ways to use hilbertSamuelFunction:
==================================

  * "hilbertSamuelFunction(Ideal,Module,ZZ)"
  * "hilbertSamuelFunction(Ideal,Module,ZZ,ZZ)"
  * "hilbertSamuelFunction(Module,ZZ)"
  * "hilbertSamuelFunction(Module,ZZ,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note hilbertSamuelFunction: hilbertSamuelFunction, is a *note
method function: (Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this document is in LocalRings/doc.m2:371:0.

