setMaxIdeal -- set the maximal ideal for local ring methods
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setMaxIdeal I
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, a maximal ideal of the ring R
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, same ideal as input

Description
===========

The function adds new structure to the ring which specifies a maximal ideal
which allows the user to employ local ring methods.
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[x,y,z,w,SkewCommutative=>true]   |
|                                                   |
|o1 = R                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing, 4 skew commutative variable(s)|
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : setMaxIdeal(ideal(x,y,z,w))                   |
|                                                   |
|o2 = ideal (x, y, z, w)                            |
|                                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                    |
+---------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note localComplement: localComplement, -- find the splitting of the target
    of a map
  * *note localsyz: localsyz, -- find syzygies
  * *note localMingens: localMingens, -- finds a minimal set of generators
  * *note localModulo: localModulo, -- find the pre-image (pullback) of image
    of a map over a local ring
  * *note localPrune: localPrune, -- find a minimal presentation
  * *note localResolution: localResolution, -- find a resolution over a local
    ring
  * *note residueMap: LocalRing, -- The class of all local rings
  * *note maxIdeal: LocalRing, -- The class of all local rings

