localComplement -- find the splitting of the target of a map
************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        localComplement m
  * Inputs:
      * m, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing a homomorphism
        of free modules over a local ring
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the complement of the image of
        the homomorphism represented by m

Description
===========

The function finds a splitting of the target of m as a direct sum of the image
of m and the image of the output.
+------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[x,y]        |
|                              |
|o1 = R                        |
|                              |
|o1 : PolynomialRing           |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : m = matrix{{x,y-1},{0,x}}|
|                              |
|o2 = | x y-1 |                |
|     | 0 x   |                |
|                              |
|             2      2         |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : setMaxIdeal(ideal(x,y))  |
|                              |
|o3 = ideal (x, y)             |
|                              |
|o3 : Ideal of R               |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : localComplement m        |
|                              |
|o4 = | 0 |                    |
|     | 1 |                    |
|                              |
|             2      1         |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note setMaxIdeal: setMaxIdeal, -- set the maximal ideal for local ring
    methods
  * *note localsyz: localsyz, -- find syzygies
  * *note localMingens: localMingens, -- finds a minimal set of generators
  * *note localModulo: localModulo, -- find the pre-image (pullback) of image
    of a map over a local ring
  * *note localPrune: localPrune, -- find a minimal presentation
  * *note localResolution: localResolution, -- find a resolution over a local
    ring
  * *note residueMap: LocalRing, -- The class of all local rings
  * *note maxIdeal: LocalRing, -- The class of all local rings

Ways to use localComplement:
============================

  * "localComplement(Matrix)"

