localPrune -- find a minimal presentation
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        localPrune M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,

Description
===========

The output is a minimal presentation of the input.
+------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=QQ[a,b]                      |
|                                    |
|o1 = R                              |
|                                    |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : setMaxIdeal ideal gens R       |
|                                    |
|o2 = ideal (a, b)                   |
|                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                     |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : m = matrix{{a-1,a,b},{a-1,a,b}}|
|                                    |
|o3 = | a-1 a b |                    |
|     | a-1 a b |                    |
|                                    |
|             2      3               |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : prune m                        |
|                                    |
|o4 = | a-1 a b |                    |
|     | a-1 a b |                    |
|                                    |
|             2      3               |
|o4 : Matrix R  <-- R                |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : localPrune image m             |
|                                    |
|      1                             |
|o5 = R                              |
|                                    |
|o5 : R-module, free, degrees {1}    |
+------------------------------------+

